{
  "domainId": "INSURANCE_DOMAIN",
  "name": "I2. Plan profitability and medical loss ratio",
  "rawText": "# Do you know which insurance plans generate the most premium revenue and how much of that revenue is consumed by medical claims?\n#  - Which insurance plans generate the highest premium revenue?\n#  - Which insurance plans have the highest medical loss ratios?\n#  - How much are we paying out in medical claims compared with the premiums collected?\n#  - Which insurance tiers have the greatest financial exposure from paid claims?\n#  - Which insurance plans have the highest number of claims?\n#  - Which insurance plans experience the most denied claims?\n#  - Are high-revenue insurance plans also generating disproportionately high medical costs?\n#  - Which plans collect substantial premiums but have relatively low claim payouts?\n#  - How does medical loss ratio vary across different insurance tiers?\n#  - Which insurance plans should we review to improve financial performance and manage claim costs?\n# __________________________________________________\n\nInsurancePlans: Name Plan,\n    Tier,\n    Policies.Count() PolicyCount,\n    Round(IfNull(Policies.Sum(PremiumPayments.SumIf(Amount, Status = \u003CPaid\u003E)), 0), 2) PremiumRevenue,\n    Round(IfNull(Policies.Sum(Claims.Sum(PaidAmount)), 0), 2) ClaimsPaid,\n    Policies.Sum(Claims.Count()) ClaimCount,\n    Policies.Sum(Claims.CountIf(Status = \u003CDenied\u003E)) DeniedClaims,\n    (100 * IfNull(Policies.Sum(Claims.Sum(PaidAmount)), 0)\n        / NullIf(Policies.Sum(PremiumPayments.SumIf(Amount, Status = \u003CPaid\u003E)), 0)).Round(2) MedicalLossRatioPercent\n  Order MedicalLossRatioPercent DESC\n  Take 10",
  "id": "Insurance 2. Plan profitability and medical loss ratio",
  "isBuiltin": false,
  "contexts": {},
